chapter.v:
Your throne, 


O God,, 


is forever and ever. The scepter of your kingdom is a scepter of uprightness;

you have 


loved righteousness, 


and hated wickedness. Therefore God, your God, has anointed you with the oil of gladness beyond your companions;

your robes 


are all, 


fragrant with myrrh and aloes and cassia. From ivory palaces stringed instruments make you glad;
